#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:357
msgid "Noise Functions"
msgstr "Funções de Ruído"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:360
msgid "float **cellnoise** ( vector v )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise** ( vector v )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:361
msgid "float **cellnoise1** ( float x )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise1** ( float x )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:362
msgid "float **cellnoise2** ( float x, float y )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise2** ( float x, float y )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:363
msgid "float **cellnoise3** ( float x, float y, float z )"
msgstr "float **cellnoise3** ( float x, float y, float z )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:364
msgid "color **ccellnoise** ( vector v )"
msgstr "color **ccellnoise** ( vector v )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:366
msgid ""
"``cellnoise`` generates a field of constant colored cubes based on the "
"integer location. This is the same as the `PRMan cellnoise function <https://"
"renderman.pixar.com/resources/RenderMan_20/cellnoise.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"O ``cellnoise`` gera um campo de cubos coloridos constantes com base na "
"localização inteira. Isto é igual à `função 'cellnoise' do PRMan <https://"
"renderman.pixar.com/resources/RenderMan_20/cellnoise.html>`_."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:370
msgid "``ccellnoise`` outputs color cellnoise."
msgstr "O ``ccellnoise`` devolve o ruído em células de cores."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:372
msgid ""
"float **fbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **fbm** ( vector v, int oitavas=6, float lacunas=2, float ganho=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:373
msgid ""
"color **cfbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **cfbm** ( vector v, int oitavas=6, float lacunas=2, float ganho=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:374
msgid ""
"vector **vfbm** ( vector v, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, float "
"gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **vfbm** ( vector v, int oitavas=6, float lacunas=2, float ganho=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:375
msgid ""
"float **fbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **fbm4** ( vector v, int oitavas=6, float lacunas=2, float ganho=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:376
msgid ""
"color **cfbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **cfbm4** ( vector v, int oitavas=6, float lacunas=2, float ganho=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:377
msgid ""
"vector **vfbm4** ( vector v, float time, int octaves=6, float lacunarity=2, "
"float gain=0.5 )"
msgstr ""
"float **cfbm4** ( vector v, int oitavas=6, float lacunas=2, float ganho=0.5 )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:379
msgid ""
"``fbm`` (Fractal Brownian Motion) is a multi-frequency noise function. The "
"base frequency is the same as the ``noise`` function. The total number of "
"frequencies is controlled by ``octaves``. The ``lacunarity`` is the spacing "
"between the frequencies - a value of 2 means each octave is twice the "
"previous frequency. The ``gain`` controls how much each frequency is scaled "
"relative to the previous frequency."
msgstr ""
"O ``fbm`` (Fractal Brownian Motion - Movimento Fractal de Brown) é uma "
"função de ruído multi-frequências. A frequência de base é igual à da função "
"``noise``. O número total de frequências é controlado pelas ``oitavas``. As "
"``lacunas`` é o intervalo entre as frequências - um valor de 2 significa que "
"cada oitava é duas vezes a frequência anterior. O ``ganho`` controla qual o "
"ajuste da escala de cada frequência face à frequência anterior."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:388
msgid "``cfbm`` and ``cfbm4`` outputs color noise."
msgstr "O ``cfbm`` e o ``cfbm4`` devolvem o ruído da cor."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:390
msgid "``vfbm`` and ``vfbm4`` outputs vector noise."
msgstr "O ``vfbm`` e o ``vfbm4`` devolvem o ruído do vector."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:391
msgid "float **hash** ( float seed1, [float seed2, ...] )"
msgstr "float **hash** ( float base1, [float base2, ...] )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:393
msgid ""
"Like ``rand``, but with no internal seeds. Any number of seeds may be given "
"and the result will be a random function based on all the seeds."
msgstr ""
"Como o ``rand``, mas sem valores de base internos. Poderá indicar qualquer "
"número de valores de base e o resultado será uma função aleatória com base "
"em todos os valores de base."

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:396
msgid "float **noise** ( vector v )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( vector v )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:397
msgid "float **noise** ( float x, float y )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( float x, float y )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:398
msgid "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:399
msgid "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z, float w )"
msgstr "float **noise** ( float x, float y, float z, float w )"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:400
msgid "color **cnoise** ( vector v)"
msgstr "color **cnoise** ( vector v)"

#: ../../reference_manual/seexpr.rst:401
